# Orbital Congestion Simulator

Vite + TypeScript + Three.js + satellite.js (SGP4). Live data is static `public/data/tle.json` (CelesTrak), not a live tracking API.

## Entry & ownership

- Boot: `src/main.ts` → TLE load → `appState` → Layout panels → `SceneManager` → deep link / Kessler / how-to
- State: `src/state/appState.ts` — single store; selections are mutually exclusive (object / event / conjunction)
- Scene: `src/scene/SceneManager.ts` — rAF loop, propagation worker, VERIFY + historical replay overlays
- UI: `LeftPanel` (filters, alerts, events), `RightPanel` (detail / Spotter), `TimeControls`, `KesslerPanel`, `HowToGuide`
- Catalog refresh: `npm run fetch-tle` → `scripts/fetch-tle.mjs` → daily GitHub Action

## Simulation clocks (do not mix)

Priority for displayed time: **VERIFY** → **event replay** → **global live/historical**.  
Spotter always uses **wall-clock**, never sim speed. Event replay uses geo lerp to a verified impact point (old TLEs are not back-propagated).

## Hard gotchas

- Thin CelesTrak fetches must not ship: `fetch-tle.mjs` refuses write if total/stations/active/debris below mins; leave previous `tle.json` intact
- Deep link clear: URL with no valid `?object=`/`?event=` must call `clearHistoricalEventSelection()` (not only `stopEventReplay`)
- Globe pick: prefer higher orbit among near-stacked hits (`screenPick.ts`) — LEO must not steal GEO clicks
- i18n: add keys to all of `en|tr|de|ru|zh`; `npm run check:i18n` fails CI on drift
- “New to this catalog” = `firstSeenAt` in our TLE list (14d), not launch date — see `docs/NEW_OBJECTS.md`

